    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (72.07) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.70) anchor the offense as our clear-cut top plays. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Phillips, where his base projections are bolstered by a solid SP_xERA of 4.52 and optimal order placement. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-ceiling matchup against Bradish; while his dynamic platoon split against a right-hander carries a slight negative, his raw power profile and the 4.45 xERA of the opposing starter keep him in the elite tier. **Josh Jung** (59.95) and **Gunnar Henderson** (58.62) round out our most potent hitters, with **Gunnar Henderson** specifically drawing a +14% boost for his platoon advantage, helping offset the moderate challenge posed by Miles.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Coby Mayo**, whose 38.12 score fell just short of the 40-point threshold required to displace **Miguel Vargas** or **Jackson Merrill**. Despite **Coby Mayo** showing potential, the combination of a tough 3.20 xERA from Miles and a downward adjustment for his platoon matchup forced him to the bench to preserve our limited game caps. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (58.15) holds his spot in the OF5 slot due to favorable park and SP skill factors, even with a minor efficiency penalty related to the opposing catcher's pop time.\n\nWe are monitoring the starting lineups for **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** closely, as any deviation from the projected batting order could impact their efficiency scores, which currently sit in the marginal 48\u201349 range. The risk profile remains stable today, though we are wary of the aggressive pitching from Miles against **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**. As we navigate the season, we remain cautious with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on our active core to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven SB and AVG categories.",
